    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dentĭcŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		dim.
		dens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little tooth</i> (not ante-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 28,
			6</span></i>; Ap. Mag. p. 278, 9.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An agricultural implement with teeth</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Pall. Jun. 2,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			archit., <i>a modillion</i>, 
			<i>dental</i>, a small ornament between the frieze and
			the larmier, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
